course: dictionary
lesson: 5740
title: Loud and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word loud has more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one you need. Most often it means making a big sound that is easy to hear. «A bigger vibration makes a louder sound» is about sound, so loud means noisy there. Ask yourself: what is the sentence talking about?
explain: Loud can also describe colour or clothes. «Loud and warm can go together» means bright colours that catch the eye, not noise. Louder and loudest compare how big a sound is, and «out loud» or «aloud» means so that others can hear, as in «read it out loud».
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence in place of loud. If it still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Loud means making a big sound that is easy to hear.
fact: Loud can also mean very bright, as in loud colours or clothes that catch the eye.
fact: «Out loud» and «aloud» mean so that others can hear: read it out loud.
fact: Louder and loudest compare how big sounds are, and loudness is measured in decibels.
fact: Very loud noise can hurt your ears, so keep your voice at a kind, inside level.
exercise: «A bigger vibration makes a louder sound.» In this sentence, what does louder mean? | *Making a bigger sound that is easier to hear | Talking more and more noisily all day | Faster and higher | Brighter and more colourful
exercise: «Loud and warm can go together.» Here, loud describes what? | *Bright colours that catch the eye | A crack in a nut | A person who talks a lot | Big sounds from a radio
exercise: Which phrase means so that others can hear? | rarely | softly | silently | *aloud
test: «A howler monkey booms so loud it fills the building.» What does loud show here? | A monkey that talks a lot to people | Bright fur that catches the eye | A quiet little squeak | *A huge sound that is easy to hear
test: Which sentence uses loud to mean bright? | «Read it out loud, please.» | «A loud crack does not always mean a break.» | *«The loud shirt was red, yellow and green.» | «Speak up, not so loud.»
exam: In «A tummy rumble is louder when the stomach is empty», which meaning of loud is used? | *Making a big sound that is easy to hear | Very bright, catching the eye | So that others can hear, read aloud | A person who talks a lot and noisily
